.TH MIME 2
.SH NAME
mime \- MIME message parsing and transfer-encoding decoding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "mime.m";
mime := load Mime Mime->PATH;
Part: import mime;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Mime
parses an RFC 822 message with MIME (RFC 2045) extensions into a tree of
.B Part
values and decodes each part's transfer encoding.
.PP
.B init
must be called once.
.B parse
takes a whole message (headers, a blank line, then the body) and returns
its root
.BR Part .
.PP
A
.B Part
has the content type
.B ctype
(\c
.BR type/subtype ,
lower-cased), the content-type
.B params
(\c
.B charset,
.BR boundary ,
\&...), the
.B disp
(content-disposition), the attachment
.B filename
if any, the transfer
.B encoding
and the part
.BR headers .
For a leaf part
.B body
holds the
.I decoded
content; for a
.B multipart/*
part
.B parts
holds the sub-parts and
.B body
is nil.
.PP
The methods are
.B ismultipart
(true for a
.B multipart/*
part),
.B param
(look up a content-type parameter), and
.B find
(the first leaf part of a given
.BR ctype ,
searched depth-first \(em for example the
.B text/plain
alternative of a message).
.PP
.B decode
decodes a body under a named transfer encoding:
.BR base64 ,
.B quoted-printable
and
.BR 7bit / 8bit / binary
(returned unchanged).
.PP
.B hdrdecode
decodes the RFC 2047 encoded-words
.RB ( "=?charset?B?...?=" ,
.BR "=?charset?Q?...?=" )
that appear in
.B Subject
and address headers, leaving surrounding text as is; the decoded bytes
are returned as received (no character-set conversion).
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/lib/mime.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR upasfs (4),
.IR upas-fetch (1)
.SH BUGS
No character-set conversion is done \(em decoded bytes are returned as
received (UTF-8 displays correctly; other charsets are not transcoded).
